# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Root .dev.vars — template. Copy to `.dev.vars` and fill in. `.dev.vars` is
# gitignored.
#
# This file is committed and must NEVER hold a real value.
#
# These two are WORKER SECRETS, not build configuration, and they are a
# different mechanism from .env:
#
#   .env       read by Node at build time (the migration scripts, Vite)
#   .dev.vars  read by `wrangler dev` and by web/src/middleware.js, and it is
#              the LOCAL stand-in for `wrangler secret put`
#
# In every deployed environment they come from Cloudflare, never from a file:
#
#   wrangler secret put PRIVATE_PAGE_PASSWORD  --config wrangler.prod.jsonc
#   wrangler secret put PRIVATE_SESSION_SECRET --config wrangler.prod.jsonc
#
# Both configs declare them under `secrets.required`, so a deploy fails fast
# while either is unset.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The password visitors type at the /poac gate.
#
# Read by worker/index.mjs. Non-empty; while it is absent every protected route
# answers 401 and the login endpoint answers 503, so a missing value LOCKS the
# page rather than opening it.
#
# It is part of the session signing key, so CHANGING IT SIGNS EVERYBODY OUT
# IMMEDIATELY. That is the only revocation a shared password has.
#
# Hand it to the client out of band — not in this repo, not in a commit
# message, not in the Sanity dataset, not in a ticket.
PRIVATE_PAGE_PASSWORD=

# HMAC signing material for the session cookie. Read by worker/index.mjs.
#
# MUST BE AT LEAST 32 CHARACTERS and randomly generated — the login handler
# answers 503 rather than issuing a session otherwise. Generate it, never
# compose it:
#
#   openssl rand -base64 32
#
# NEVER derive it from the password, and never reuse it between environments.
# Nothing secret rides in the cookie (the signed payload is only the expiry),
# so this value's whole job is to make a forged cookie impossible.
PRIVATE_SESSION_SECRET=
